{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The fifth time</b><br>איכה תרעה. It is [its meaning is a question of place, like the meaning of איכה there] like the sense of איפה:" "שלמה. The shin in place of אשר, like the shin of 'you speak with me':" "כעטיה. It means skipping about, and he said, thus ויעט העם. Others say, ashamed, as in על שפם יעטה. But the correct view in my eyes is that it is from ועוטך עטה; like a garment, יעטה:" "<b>The second time</b><br>She returns to her beloved and says to him: Tell me where you graze your flock and where you rest them, lest I wander about — [that] I might mingle with the flocks of your companions the shepherds:"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The citation ועוטך עטה is textually obscure; rendered hyper-literally as it appears in the Hebrew.", 3 "Resolved the abbreviated אפחד(ה) as 'lest I wander about'; the parenthetical heh in the source suggests a textual variant."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:49.530406319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}